1. Pointer to an Integer Variable
Problem Statement

Write a C program to declare a pointer, initialize it with the address of an integer variable, and
display the value and address of the variable using both the variable and the pointer.
Program

#include <stdio.h>
int main()
{
int num;
int *ptr;
printf("Enter an integer: ");
scanf("%d", &num);
ptr = &num;
printf("\nUsing Variable:\n");
printf("Value of variable = %d\n", num);
printf("Address of variable = %p\n", (void *)&num);
printf("\nUsing Pointer:\n");
printf("Value using pointer = %d\n", *ptr);
printf("Address using pointer = %p\n", (void *)ptr);
return 0;
}
